@commise/features-recipes — native public-discovery result card, the twin of the web leaf
(`docs/design/uiOverhaul/buildSpec.md` §4.1): the shared {@link RecipeCard} in the variant the host decided, with the
Discover footer (the author and the Save a copy icon button) in its `footer` slot. The card's link covers the recipe;
the footer sits beside it, so the Save a copy control stays its own accessible element.

@commise/features-recipes/editor — the web editor's alert for a write the outbox parked (build spec §7.8,
ADR-0057: it waits for the cook): what happened, and what the cook can do. Words are `staff-ux-engineer`'s (slice 7).

Presentational: props → JSX.

@commise/features-recipes/editor — the native editor's alert for a write the outbox parked (build spec §7.8,
ADR-0057). Same props as the web leaf.

Presentational: props → JSX.

@commise/features-recipes/editor — the Ready line of Photos & publish (build spec §7.7 item 3): always
there, so the cook reads whether Publish will go through before pressing it. "Ready to publish." is plain text;
"Fix {n} things to publish" is a ghost button that takes the cook to the first section that needs it (SC 2.4.4).
The action bar's polite line is the one that announces, so this one is not a live region.

Presentational: props → JSX. The native leaf is `./PublishLine.native.tsx`.

@commise/features-recipes/editor — the native Ready line of Photos & publish; the mirror of
`PublishLine.tsx`. Plain text when ready, a ghost button to the first section that needs it otherwise.

Presentational: props → JSX.

@commise/features-recipes/editor — the native one-page recipe editor (build spec §7, §7.12; owner decisions
D1, D2, D3, D12): the header, the section index, the four sections, the action bar and the notices, over the editor's
lifecycle (`useRecipeEditor`). Create and edit are this one screen.

ORCHESTRATION of the screen: it owns the screen's one `ScrollHost` and its one vertical scroller, and draws what
`useEditorPage` decides — the same model the web leaf draws. Native adds what its platform alone has:

- each section is a DIRECT child of the scroller's content, reporting its layout to the host (blueprint A7);
- a jump moves the SCREEN-READER cursor to the section's heading (the host holds no heading refs);
- the action bar sits outside the scroller in the thumb zone, and becomes the scroller's last content when the
  header and the bar together would take more than half the frame (`usePinnedFooter`; `compactHeightLayout.md` A1);
- while the keyboard is open the section bar hides, so the header alone holds the top edge (build spec §7.1). The
  pinning measures the header alone, so the bar hiding never moves the action bar back;
- an ingredient field whose list opens behind the bar or the keyboard is revealed (`useFieldRevealHost`), over the
  host's one scroller; and the cook's drag on that scroller closes an open food list unless it began on the list
  (`useScrollerDragHost`).

No back-to-top control (D3): a second tap on the tab and the iOS status-bar tap do that job. × never asks.

@commise/features-recipes/editor — the web editor's resume notice (build spec §7.3): a published recipe has
device changes from an earlier visit, with Save changes and Discard.

Presentational: props → JSX.

@commise/features-recipes/filters — the native applied-filter chips, the twin of the web leaf
(`docs/design/uiOverhaul/buildSpec.md` §4.4): each filter in force as a removable input chip named "Remove {filter}
filter", in a scrolling row, then Clear all (ghost) once two or more apply. With nothing applied it draws nothing.

Presentational: it draws the applied-filter chips and reports removals.

@commise/features-recipes/foodPage — `YourFoodsScreen` (native): the cook's own foods as a stack pushes it from
Profile (private foods spec F19). The orchestration component: the read is `useOwnFoods`, the body is `YourFoodsList`;
this adds the pinned Back and the large title. The host owns the route. Styled with Tamagui only.

@commise/features-recipes/form — `FoodDetailsSheet` (native): a quiet row's details, opened from its `⋯`
Food details (build spec §7.5.1). The React Native leaf of `./FoodDetailsSheet.tsx`.

Presentational: it frames the row's panel body over the field group's Food details view.

@commise/features-recipes/form — `GroupNameField` (web): the inline name field of "+ Add a group" and Rename
group (build spec §7.5.5): a labelled field, Save and Cancel. Enter saves; Escape cancels. It takes focus as it shows.

Presentational: `props → JSX` over the field's view (`GroupNameFieldView`).

@commise/features-recipes/form — `GroupNameField` (native): the inline name field of "+ Add a group" and
Rename group (build spec §7.5.5). The React Native leaf of `./GroupNameField.tsx`: the keyboard's done key saves.

Presentational: `props → JSX` over the field's view (`GroupNameFieldView`).

@commise/features-recipes/form — `IngredientsNutritionTotal` (web): the Ingredients section's running total
(build spec §7.5.6), at the section's foot and at the section index's rail foot. Loading is skeleton text (still under
`prefers-reduced-motion`), never a partial figure; failed is the failure and, where the host offers it, Try again;
ready is "612 cal per serving · 7 of 9 counted", or "Nutrition appears as you match ingredients." — never "0 cal".

Presentational: `props → JSX` over the total's view (`nutritionTotalViewOf`).

@commise/features-recipes/form — `PastedReadingRow` (native): the React Native leaf of
`./PastedReadingRow.tsx`, on the same props and the same words (`pasteStatusCopy.ts`). Painted from the theme's roles,
so it reads in both themes (D15). The one action sits on its own line, so nothing wraps inside a control at 320 px.

@commise/features-recipes/form — `PasteMatchSummary` (native): the React Native leaf of
`./PasteMatchSummary.tsx`, on the same props and words: "Added 8 lines", then one muted paragraph of the counts and the
rule, on the page rather than a fill card (U4). Painted from the theme's roles (D15).

@commise/features-recipes/form — the web `ShortlistPanel`, rows 6 and 7's panel (SPECIFY.1 rows 6 and 7).

Orchestration: `useShortlistPanel` searches, derives the view and makes the pick; this leaf hands the view to the
presentational web `CandidatesPanelBody`.

@commise/features-recipes/import — `ImportLineList` (native): the React Native leaf of `./ImportLineList.tsx`,
on the same props: the ONE shared matched-line list (`MatchLineList`) under the recipe-with-nothing-to-fix sentence.
Painted from the theme's roles (D15).

@commise/features-recipes/import — `ImportReviewRail` (native): the React Native leaf of
`./ImportReviewRail.tsx`, drawn beside the review step at the wide container class (1194). The current recipe is
`selected`, filled and ringed in the selected edge (U10); a skipped one says so in its own words; each row keeps the 44 pt touch floor.

@commise/features-recipes/import — `ImportSummary` (native): the React Native leaf of `./ImportSummary.tsx`,
on the same words (`summaryCopy.ts`). Each row's action sits after its words and wraps under them at 320 dp rather
than squeezing them; Choose foods fills the width. The nutrition coverage follows at the wide container class (1194).

@commise/features-recipes/ingredientMatching — `MatchLineText` (native): the React Native leaf of
`./MatchLineText.tsx`, in the 16 px `body` role (the owner's type-scale ruling). The measure is set in the semibold face rather than with a
`fontWeight`, which Android would synthesise (`nativeTokens.type`). Painted from the theme's roles (D15).

