implementations.moduleDoc:
@commise/features-recipes — the web create entry (build spec §3.4; owner decision D4; blueprint Part C slice
8): "New recipe", which opens the empty editor in ONE tap. Paste lives in the editor's Ingredients section, so there
is no menu. After link or photo import ship, the same control opens a chooser, which gets its own SPECIFY pass.

Three forms of the one control, by where it is drawn (display derivation, `RecipeCreateButtonProps.appearance`):
- `fab` (the default): the design system's floating `CreateFab`, with its rules (it shrinks on scroll, hides with the
  keyboard and in first run, and is gone from 840 px);
- `sidebar`: the expanded web sidebar's full-width primary "New recipe" (§3.2);
- `rail`: the collapsed sidebar's 56 px round icon button, named by its label, with the design system's `Tooltip` on
  hover and on focus that stays while hovered and that Escape dismisses (SC 1.4.13). The tooltip is for sight only; the
  name carries it.

@commise/features-recipes — the native create entry (build spec §3.4; owner decision D4): the floating "New
recipe" `CreateFab`, which opens the empty editor in ONE tap. Paste lives in the editor's Ingredients section, so
there is no menu. Native has no sidebar, so the floating form is its only form and `appearance` is not read.

@commise/features-recipes — the header the web version history's LOADING and FAILED states share (D3, D13;
`docs/design/uiOverhaul/buildSpec.md` §6.6).

The SAME `LargeTitleHeader` the settled list draws — the back control and the title — so the page does not move when
the history lands, and a failed read still has its way back in its usual place.

Presentational: props → JSX. The header's words are the list's own. Its Back is the eyebrow from 840; below it the page's
pinned bar carries the same `back`, which the caller builds once (`versionBackOf`).
